+*   **Ray Casting:** For a ray $R(t) = O + tD$, the color $C$ and opacity $\alpha$ are computed by integrating along the ray path through cell $i$:
+    $$ C = \sum_{i} c_i \alpha_i \prod_{j < i} (1 - \alpha_j) $$
+    $$ \alpha = \sum_{i} \alpha_i \prod_{j < i} (1 - \alpha_j) $$
+    Where $c_i$ and $\alpha_i$ are the color and opacity of the $i$-th sample, derived from the scalar value $v_i$ via the transfer function $TF(v_i) \rightarrow (c_i, \alpha_i)$ [S1, G].
 
